--
N5008 [namespace.memdef]/2: a member of a namespace may be defined outside
it by a qualified name (`template <class, class...> class fmt::arg_store
{};'); [namespace.def]/2: a later `namespace fmt { }' is an extension of
the SAME namespace; [basic.lookup.qual.general]/1: `fmt::' then names that
one namespace.  After the qualified class template definition followed by
the reopening, the front end reported "scope 'fmt' is ambiguous" and
rejected the unit, because the qualified definition left the current
scope inside fmt and the reopening created fmt::fmt; either ingredient alone is fine.  This is libstdc++ 13's
<format>: `template<typename _Context, typename... _Args> class
__format::_Arg_store' is defined at namespace std scope and std::__format
reopened later, so the four inline std::vformat overloads
(`__format::_Str_sink<char> __buf;', format:3784-3811) are dropped;
test_libstdcxx.desc includes <format>.  Header-free (from the cvise
reduction in /tmp/r163/red/kb_K).  Fails on the round-163 build bin52.
